Lots of ports

IPv4 sockets
- server IP address > protocol (TCP or UDP) > server application port number
- client IP address > protocol > client port number

Non-ephemeral ports or permanent port numbers from Ports between 0 through 1,023 and usually on a server or service | also known as static or fixed port
Ephemeral ports or temporary port numbers from Ports 1,024 through 65,535 and determined in real-time by the client


=====================================================================================================================================================================================================================================================

Port numbers

- TCP and UDP ports can be any number between 0 and 65,535
- most servers use non-ephemeral port numbers
- TCP port numbers aren't the same as UDP port numbers
- source port is dynamic or random
- destination port is static
